WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.850 --> 00:00:05.650
This special episode of Office Ladies is brought to you by Hershey's Kisses.
本期《办公室女士》特别节目由好时之吻巧克力为您呈现。

2
00:00:05.850 --> 00:00:10.810
So earlier this year, we recorded our first ever live Office Ladies episode.
今年早些时候，我们录制了《办公室女士》有史以来的第一场现场节目。

3
00:00:11.130 --> 00:00:13.010
People flew in from all over.
大家从各地飞来参加。

4
00:00:13.170 --> 00:00:14.310
It was so crazy.
真是太疯狂了。

5
00:00:14.910 --> 00:00:20.290
This is some of our, like, OG Office Ladies fans that have been with us from the very beginning.
这里面有一些从一开始就陪伴我们的《办公室女士》元老级粉丝。

6
00:00:20.290 --> 00:00:22.110
We got to meet so many of you.
我们见到了你们当中的许多人。

7
00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:24.330
It was absolutely a blaSt.
那绝对是一段非常愉快的时光。

8
00:00:24.350 --> 00:00:28.810
And we couldn't be happier to partner with Hershey's to now bring it to you all to listen.
我们非常高兴能与好时合作，现在将这段录音呈现给大家收听。

9
00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:34.510
This collaboration is kind of perfect because later on in the episode, we are going to talk about kisses.
这次合作堪称完美，因为在节目稍后的部分，我们要聊聊“吻”这个话题。

10
00:00:34.890 --> 00:00:35.090
Yeah.
没错。

11
00:00:35.330 --> 00:00:35.910
That's right.
正是如此。

12
00:00:36.050 --> 00:00:39.990
We dive back into the debate about a certain first kiss on the office.
我们将重新探讨《办公室》中关于某个初吻的争论。

13
00:00:40.530 --> 00:00:43.390
But first, let's talk about a different kind of kiss.
但首先，让我们聊聊另一种“吻”。

14
00:00:43.630 --> 00:00:47.630
Well, you know, the holidays are a time to break out your best outfits.
你知道，节日是穿上你最漂亮衣服的时候。

15
00:00:47.670 --> 00:00:54.290
And when it comes to candy, I'm sorry, but is there a better dress treat than a Hershey's Kiss with its sparkling festive foils?
说到糖果，抱歉，还有什么比穿着闪亮节日包装纸的好时之吻更精致的甜点吗？

16
00:00:54.290 --> 00:01:03.370
This holiday season, you and your family will delight in decorating the house with Kisses chocolates dressed in shining red, green, silver foils.
这个节日季，你和家人可以用包装着红、绿、银色闪亮锡纸的好时巧克力来装饰屋子，一定会让你们感到欣喜。

17
00:01:03.510 --> 00:01:05.990
Their snowman foils are even Santa hats.
它们的雪人包装纸甚至还戴着圣诞帽。

18
00:01:06.390 --> 00:01:07.870
The Santa hats are so cute.
那些圣诞帽真是太可爱了。

19
00:01:07.890 --> 00:01:09.950
My mom stole my bag of Santa hats.
我妈偷走了我那袋戴圣诞帽的巧克力。

20
00:01:09.970 --> 00:01:10.530
Kisses.
好时之吻。

21
00:01:10.730 --> 00:01:11.330
She did.
她真的偷了。

22
00:01:11.530 --> 00:01:12.450
Story for later.
以后再讲这个故事。

23
00:01:13.470 --> 00:01:15.150
Hershey's heartwarming the world.
好时，温暖全世界。

24
00:01:15.350 --> 00:01:19.010
Learn more at www.hersheyland.com.
了解更多信息请访问 www.hersheyland.com。

25
00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:22.830
All right.
好了。

26
00:01:23.130 --> 00:01:23.910
Are you guys ready?
你们准备好了吗？

27
00:01:25.290 --> 00:01:25.750
Okay.
好的。

28
00:01:26.970 --> 00:01:28.870
Sam, can we get a theme song?
山姆，能来段主题曲吗？

29
00:01:30.010 --> 00:01:30.710
Here we go.
开始了。

30
00:01:32.450 --> 00:01:33.390
I'm Jenna Fisher.
我是珍娜·费舍尔。

31
00:01:33.670 --> 00:01:34.710
And I'm Angela Kinsey.
我是安吉拉·金赛。

32
00:01:34.830 --> 00:01:35.990
We were on The Office together.
我们曾一起出演《办公室》。

33
00:01:36.270 --> 00:01:37.230
And we're best friends.
我们是最好的朋友。

34
00:01:37.290 --> 00:01:41.050
And now we're doing the Ultimate Office rewatch podcast just for you.
现在，我们专为你制作了这档终极《办公室》重温播客。

35
00:01:41.230 --> 00:01:48.030
Each week, we will break down an episode of The Office and give exclusive behind-the-scenes stories that only two people who were there can tell you.
每周，我们都会剖析一集《办公室》，并分享只有身临其境的我们两人才能告诉你的独家幕后故事。

36
00:01:48.230 --> 00:01:49.210
We're The Office ladies.
我们是《办公室女士》。

37
00:02:04.320 --> 00:02:04.780
Goodness.
天哪。

38
00:02:04.780 --> 00:02:09.730
Oh, for being here.
噢，感谢你们来到这里。

39
00:02:09.870 --> 00:02:12.010
We know a lot of you traveled to be here.
我们知道你们很多人是特地赶来的。

40
00:02:12.270 --> 00:02:15.010
We cannot tell you how much we appreciate it.
我们无法用言语表达我们的感激之情。

41
00:02:15.810 --> 00:02:18.530
This is tears here in the first row.
第一排这里有人流泪了。

42
00:02:19.370 --> 00:02:19.810
Tears.
眼泪。

43
00:02:20.030 --> 00:02:21.330
We have some tears.
我们看到有人流泪了。

44
00:02:21.490 --> 00:02:24.730
It's going to make us cry.
这会把我们也弄哭的。

45
00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:25.590
Yeah, no, yeah.
是啊，没错，是啊。

46
00:02:26.250 --> 00:02:26.530
Wait.
等等。

47
00:02:26.750 --> 00:02:27.810
We don't have tissues.
我们没有纸巾。

48
00:02:28.030 --> 00:02:28.750
We don't have tissues.
我们没带纸巾。

49
00:02:28.930 --> 00:02:30.770
That's the one thing we didn't think of, Ange.
安吉，这是我们唯一没想到的事。

50
00:02:31.270 --> 00:02:31.490
Okay.
好吧。

51
00:02:32.110 --> 00:02:37.150
So this is our very first time recording a podcast in front of a live audience.
这是我们第一次在现场观众面前录制播客。

52
00:02:37.330 --> 00:02:37.470
Yeah.
没错。

53
00:02:37.670 --> 00:02:39.670
So, amazing.
太棒了。

54
00:02:40.350 --> 00:02:45.840
It might be flunky, but we'll get through it.
可能会有点手忙脚乱，但我们会搞定的。

55
00:02:46.160 --> 00:02:50.020
But just seeing your faces here is just making my heart beat so faSt.
看到你们在场，我的心跳得好快。

56
00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:51.560
This is so special.
这真的很特别。

57
00:02:51.880 --> 00:02:54.260
You know I have to document it for office ladies.
你们知道我得为《办公室女士》记录下这一刻。

58
00:03:02.860 --> 00:03:04.980
Will you guys say hi?
大家能打个招呼吗？

59
00:03:12.520 --> 00:03:18.100
So today, we are going to do our mailbag fan appreciation episode.
今天，我们要录制一期粉丝回馈的信箱问答节目。

60
00:03:18.100 --> 00:03:19.420
That is why you're here.
这就是你们今天到场的原因。

61
00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:20.020
Yes.
没错。

62
00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:21.880
Yes.
是的。

63
00:03:22.780 --> 00:03:28.520
You know, so many of you have written in over the years and have just shared your stories with us.
多年来，你们中有许多人写信给我们，分享你们的故事。

64
00:03:28.640 --> 00:03:29.560
I'm so emotional.
我太感动了。

65
00:03:29.560 --> 00:03:35.940
So, and we just thought it would be really fun to open up our office ladies mailbag with you all.
所以我们觉得，和大家一起打开《办公室女士》的信箱会很有趣。

66
00:03:36.260 --> 00:03:37.980
And we're just so happy you're here.
我们真的很高兴你们能来。

67
00:03:38.140 --> 00:03:38.600
Yes.
是的。

68
00:03:38.600 --> 00:03:41.520
But first, we want to introduce you to our team.
但首先，我们要向大家介绍我们的团队。

69
00:03:41.720 --> 00:03:42.980
Yes, our office ladies.
没错，我们的《办公室女士》团队。

70
00:03:44.160 --> 00:03:44.800
All right.
好的。

71
00:03:44.940 --> 00:03:47.840
So, first of all, our senior producer, Cassie Jerkins.
首先是我们的高级制作人，凯西·杰金斯。

72
00:03:48.280 --> 00:03:48.760
Cassie!
凯西！

73
00:03:49.960 --> 00:03:58.300
And we also have our editing and mixing engineer, Jordan Duffy.
还有我们的剪辑和混音工程师，乔丹·达菲。

74
00:03:58.600 --> 00:03:59.120
Jordan!
乔丹！

75
00:04:03.260 --> 00:04:05.220
And studio engineer, Sam Kiefer.
以及录音室工程师，萨姆·基弗。

76
00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:05.660
Sam!
萨姆！

77
00:04:08.540 --> 00:04:12.180
And our associate producer, Ainsley Babaco.
还有我们的助理制作人，安斯利·巴巴科。

78
00:04:12.600 --> 00:04:20.650
We also have Colin and Cody there around the corner somewhere.
科林和科迪也在角落那边。

79
00:04:20.650 --> 00:04:24.610
We have a reception little party planned for after, so you'll get to meet everyone.
我们之后安排了一个小型招待会，你们可以去见见大家。

80
00:04:24.910 --> 00:04:27.830
Everyone that helps us make the show mean so much to us.
每一位帮助我们制作节目的人对我们来说都意义非凡。

81
00:04:27.830 --> 00:04:33.570
Our merchandise team, Ileana, who does our website, everyone here at SiriusXM that helped make this happen today.
还有我们的周边团队、负责网站的伊莱亚娜，以及今天在SiriusXM帮助我们实现这一切的每一个人。

82
00:04:34.230 --> 00:04:40.310
So, we thought we would kick things off with a piece of mail about our team, a particular team member.
我们想先从一封关于我们团队成员的信开始。

83
00:04:40.730 --> 00:04:42.230
I've gotten a lot of these letters.
我收到了很多这样的信。

84
00:04:42.590 --> 00:04:44.650
You got a fan mail flurry about it.
你收到了一大堆关于这个的粉丝来信。

85
00:04:44.710 --> 00:04:46.210
I got a fan mail flurry about it.
我确实收到了一大堆粉丝来信。

86
00:04:46.510 --> 00:04:48.290
This one is from Marnie W.
这封信来自玛妮·W。

87
00:04:48.610 --> 00:04:49.730
from Dallas, baby.
来自达拉斯，宝贝。

88
00:04:50.090 --> 00:04:51.050
Is that what she wrote?
她是这么写的吗？

89
00:04:51.510 --> 00:04:52.590
Dallas, baby?
达拉斯，宝贝？

90
00:04:52.930 --> 00:04:53.310
Dallas, baby?
达拉斯，宝贝？

91
00:04:53.530 --> 00:04:53.870
Yes!
没错！

92
00:04:55.190 --> 00:05:01.690
Marnie said, hi, in the last episode I listened to, you said our associate producer is Ainsley Bubaco,
玛妮说，嗨，在上一期节目里，你们说助理制作人是安斯利·巴巴科，

93
00:05:02.130 --> 00:05:08.070
rather than Ainsley Bubaco, as you have been pronouncing it in all of the previous episodes.
而不是你们之前所有节目里一直念的那个发音。

94
00:05:08.330 --> 00:05:09.350
Oh, Marnie got ya.
噢，玛妮抓到你了。

95
00:05:10.030 --> 00:05:12.510
Did Ainsley let you know you've been saying her name?
安斯利有告诉你，你一直把她的名字念错了吗？

96
00:05:13.650 --> 00:05:19.110
I've been intrigued by her name ever since I first heard it on your show, and I want to know all about this, please.
自从在你们节目里听到她的名字，我就一直很好奇，我想了解关于这名字的一切，拜托了。

97
00:05:20.230 --> 00:05:21.430
Marnie, I'm going to tell you.
玛妮，我这就告诉你。

98
00:05:21.750 --> 00:05:21.990
Yeah.
没错。

99
00:05:23.410 --> 00:05:26.170
I have known Ainsley for going on 10 years.
我和安斯利认识快10年了。

100
00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:30.230
We had the same acting coach when I was working on my book, The Actor's Life.
我在写《演员的生活》那本书时，我们用的是同一个表演教练。

101
00:05:30.390 --> 00:05:31.450
She was one of my readers.
她曾是我的读者之一。

102
00:05:31.730 --> 00:05:33.890
She did the transcriptions for me.
她帮我做过转录工作。

103
00:05:34.490 --> 00:05:36.090
We've been friends a long time.
我们认识很久了，是老朋友。

104
00:05:36.650 --> 00:05:41.990
She joined the office ladies team and is still doing our transcriptions.
她加入了《办公室女士》团队，至今仍在负责我们的转录工作。

105
00:05:42.210 --> 00:05:43.370
She helps us with our outlines.
她还帮我们整理大纲。

106
00:05:43.370 --> 00:05:45.250
Okay, here's the thing.
好吧，事情是这样的。

107
00:05:45.430 --> 00:05:50.250
In all of these years of knowing her, I never had a reason to say her last name to her face.
认识她这么多年，我从来没理由当面叫出她的姓氏。

108
00:05:50.550 --> 00:05:50.890
What?
什么？

109
00:05:51.710 --> 00:05:53.530
Because, listen, this is a Southern thing.
因为，听着，这是南方人的习惯。

110
00:05:53.730 --> 00:05:55.790
Like, my mom's friend is Sue Dean.
比如，我妈妈的朋友叫苏·迪恩（Sue Dean）。

111
00:05:55.990 --> 00:05:56.910
Her last name is Dean.
她的姓是迪恩。

112
00:05:57.010 --> 00:05:57.870
We all say Sue Dean.
我们都叫她苏·迪恩。

113
00:05:58.190 --> 00:05:59.270
That's her name, Sue Dean.
那就是她的名字，苏·迪恩。

114
00:05:59.270 --> 00:06:01.870
But you don't go around saying, hi, Angela Kinsey.
但你不会到处去说，嗨，安吉拉·金赛（Angela Kinsey）。

115
00:06:02.010 --> 00:06:02.370
I don't.
我不会那样做。

116
00:06:02.630 --> 00:06:03.010
Hi, Jenna Fisher.
嗨，珍娜·费舍（Jenna Fisher）。

117
00:06:03.150 --> 00:06:03.910
Hi, Sam Kiefer.
嗨，萨姆·基弗（Sam Kiefer）。

118
00:06:04.230 --> 00:06:04.530
Hi.
嗨。

119
00:06:04.530 --> 00:06:13.210
I never had occasion to do this until we are at a party celebrating our 100th episode of Office Ladies.
直到我们在庆祝《办公室女士》第一百集的派对上，我才有了机会这样做。

120
00:06:13.450 --> 00:06:13.750
Yes.
没错。

121
00:06:15.190 --> 00:06:18.550
We threw a fun dinner party because we love a party.
我们举办了一场有趣的晚宴，因为我们热爱派对。

122
00:06:19.130 --> 00:06:21.530
And Jenna and I thought we would get up and thank our team.
珍娜和我想着要站起来感谢我们的团队。

123
00:06:21.530 --> 00:06:30.290
And that's when Ainsley was like, by the way, you've been saying my last name wrong for a lot of episodes.
就在那时，安斯利（Ainsley）说，顺便提一下，你们在很多集里都把我的姓读错了。

124
00:06:30.290 --> 00:06:33.870
I was like, Ainsley, you've been listening to them.
我说，安斯利，你一直在听这些节目啊。

125
00:06:33.870 --> 00:06:35.810
You've been transcribing them.
你一直在做转录工作。

126
00:06:36.370 --> 00:06:37.390
Ainsley, come here.
安斯利，过来。

127
00:06:39.430 --> 00:06:39.950
Why?
为什么？

128
00:06:40.350 --> 00:06:42.770
Why did you wait so long to tell us?
你为什么等了这么久才告诉我们？

129
00:06:43.450 --> 00:06:44.650
A couple of reasons.
有几个原因。

130
00:06:44.910 --> 00:06:46.610
One, I'm very polite.
第一，我非常有礼貌。

131
00:06:48.610 --> 00:06:53.450
Two, I knew that I had never said my last name to you, so you didn't know any better.
第二，我知道我从未当面告诉你我的姓氏，所以你并不知道正确的读法。

132
00:06:53.810 --> 00:06:58.990
And three, the show is, you know, a train that has left this station.
第三，节目就像一列已经发车的火车，停不下来了。

133
00:06:58.990 --> 00:07:00.750
It's already documented.
它已经被记录在案了。

134
00:07:00.750 --> 00:07:03.930
So I just thought, why mess up a good thing?
所以我当时想，为什么要破坏一件好事呢？

135
00:07:05.130 --> 00:07:08.750
Well, I'm very happy we are now pronouncing your last name correctly.
好吧，很高兴我们现在能正确读出你的姓氏了。

136
00:07:10.570 --> 00:07:12.850
It is actually Babico.
其实是巴比科（Babico）。

137
00:07:13.150 --> 00:07:14.390
No, come on.
不，别开玩笑了。

138
00:07:14.390 --> 00:07:15.110
No.
不是吧。

139
00:07:18.940 --> 00:07:19.340
Yeah.
是真的。

140
00:07:19.640 --> 00:07:20.100
You know what?
你知道吗？

141
00:07:20.180 --> 00:07:22.060
We're going to open up a lot of mail with you guys.
我们要和大家一起拆开很多邮件。

142
00:07:25.200 --> 00:07:28.160
I want to start off with something that I know you're going to love, Angela.
我想先从一件我知道你会喜欢的事情开始，安吉拉。

143
00:07:28.440 --> 00:07:28.660
Okay.
好的。

144
00:07:29.040 --> 00:07:36.280
This is a letter from Joe V in Oregon, who did an in-depth breakdown of what it costs Jim to prank Dwight.
这是一封来自俄勒冈州乔·V（Joe V）的信，他深入分析了吉姆（Jim）捉弄德怀特（Dwight）所花费的成本。

145
00:07:37.440 --> 00:07:39.160
Over the entire series.
涵盖了整个剧集。

146
00:07:39.380 --> 00:07:41.080
Yes, I'm always saying this.
没错，我一直都在说这个。

147
00:07:41.180 --> 00:07:42.520
Like, how does he have the time?
比如，他哪来的时间？

148
00:07:42.680 --> 00:07:43.500
How does he have the money?
他哪来的钱？

149
00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:44.680
These are big pranks.
这些可都是大工程。

150
00:07:44.800 --> 00:07:46.920
Okay, he does not break down the time.
好吧，他没有分析时间成本。

151
00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:47.320
Okay.
好的。

152
00:07:47.320 --> 00:07:49.400
But he does break down the actual coSt.
但他确实细分了实际成本。

153
00:07:49.560 --> 00:07:50.980
But he made a few caveats.
但他提了几点注意事项。

154
00:07:51.260 --> 00:07:51.460
Okay.
好的。

155
00:07:51.460 --> 00:07:52.140
So I'm going to tell you.
所以我来告诉你。

156
00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:56.740
First, he only tallied the cost of Jim's pranks played on Dwight.
首先，他只统计了吉姆捉弄德怀特的成本。

157
00:07:57.100 --> 00:07:57.320
Oh.
哦。

158
